+  # Allocate an object with a collision-checked random UUID.
+  #
+  # `project.new(klass)` takes its UUID from xcodeproj's counter, which is seeded from
+  # SHA256("Pods.xcodeproj") and RESET between project generation and post_install. This runs in
+  # post_install, so its first allocation hands back 46EB2E00000000 — the UUID PBXProject already
+  # owns. The new object then overwrites the project block and Xcode refuses the whole file with
+  # "The project 'Pods' is damaged", surfacing as
+  # `-[XCSwiftPackageProductDependency _setSavedArchiveVersion:]: unrecognized selector`.
+  #
+  # Whether it collides depends on how many objects the counter has already issued, i.e. on the
+  # exact pod set — which is why adding one unrelated pod flipped this repo from building to not.
+  # Upstream fix for the same bug: maplibre-react-native#1500.
+  def new_object_with_unique_uuid(project, klass)
+    uuid = nil
+    loop do
+      uuid = SecureRandom.hex(12).upcase
+      break unless project.objects_by_uuid.key?(uuid)
+    end
+    object = klass.new(project, uuid)
+    object.initialize_defaults
+    project.objects_by_uuid[uuid] = object
+    object
+  end
+
